{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1533851938,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNDkzMDU5NzU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2760","origin":"github"},"title":"shortcut syntax to access metadata fields in the output","message":"Moved from https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/2725\n\nwe need to provide some way to shorten path to the fields in the metadata. To access any metadata field you need `{metadata[extractor][FIELD]}` to get actual field.  Since we cannot use `.` as a separator, I thought that may be we could provide support for `/` (which shouldn't be anywhere in the keys, right?) with some glob or regex semantic.  E.g. so instead of\n\n`'{path}: {metadata[annex][participant_id]!r} {metadata[annex][sex]:\u003e6} {metadata[annex][age]}'`\n\n(where `!` and `:` are just for an example) I could say\n\n'{path}: {annex/participant_id!r} {annex/sex:\u003e6} {annex/age}'\n\nor even\n\n`'{path}: {*/participant_id!r} {*/sex:\u003e6} {*/age}'`\n\nwith crash or join (`', '.join`) happening if multiple metadata records provide those fields.\nedit: may be `/` in the hierarchy should/could be used in the 'query' itself to stay consistent with the output formatting...?","files":null}]}